            object {
                id = 17
                kind = "aggregate"
                scope = 0
            }
            object {
                id = 18
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"1. I learned from my grandfather, Verus, to use good manners, and to\""
            }
            object {
                id = 19
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"put restraint on anger. 2. In the famous memory of my father I had a\""
            }
            object {
                id = 20
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"pattern of modesty and manliness. 3. Of my mother I learned to be\""
            }
            object {
                id = 21
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"pious and generous; to keep myself not only from evil deeds, but even\""
            }
            object {
                id = 22
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"from evil thoughts; and to live with a simplicity which is far from\""
            }
            object {
                id = 23
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"customary among the rich. 4. I owe it to my great-grandfather that I\""
            }
            object {
                id = 24
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"did not attend public lectures and discussions, but had good and able\""
            }
            object {
                id = 25
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"teachers at home; and I owe him also the knowledge that for things of\""
            }
            object {
                id = 26
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"this nature a man should count no expense too great.\""
            }
            object {
                id = 27
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"5. My tutor taught me not to favour either green or blue at the\""
            }
            object {
                id = 28
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"chariot races, nor, in the contests of gladiators, to be a supporter\""
            }
            object {
                id = 29
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"either of light or heavy armed. He taught me also to endure labour;\""
            }
            object {
                id = 30
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"not to need many things; to serve myself without troubling others; not\""
            }
            object {
                id = 31
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"to intermeddle in the affairs of others, and not easily to listen to\""
            }
            object {
                id = 32
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"slanders against them.\""
            }
            object {
                id = 33
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"6. Of Diognetus I had the lesson not to busy myself about vain things;\""
            }
            object {
                id = 34
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"not to credit the great professions of such as pretend to work\""
            }
            object {
                id = 35
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"wonders, or of sorcerers about their charms, and their expelling of\""
            }
            object {
                id = 36
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"Demons and the like; not to keep quails (for fighting or divination),\""
            }
            object {
                id = 37
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"nor to run after such things; to suffer freedom of speech in others,\""
            }
            object {
                id = 38
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"and to apply myself heartily to philosophy. Him also I must thank for\""
            }
            object {
                id = 39
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"my hearing first Bacchius, then Tandasis and Marcianus; that I wrote\""
            }
            object {
                id = 40
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"dialogues in my youth, and took a liking to the philosopher's pallet\""
            }
            object {
                id = 41
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"and skins, and to the other things which, by the Grecian discipline,\""
            }
            object {
                id = 42
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"belong to that profession.\""
            }
            object {
                id = 43
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"7. To Rusticus I owe my first apprehensions that my nature needed\""
            }
            object {
                id = 44
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"reform and cure; and that I did not fall into the ambition of the\""
            }
            object {
                id = 45
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"common Sophists, either by composing speculative writings or by\""
            }
            object {
                id = 46
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"declaiming harangues of exhortation in public; further, that I never\""
            }
            object {
                id = 47
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"strove to be admired by ostentation of great patience in an ascetic\""
            }
            object {
                id = 48
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"life, or by display of activity and application; that I gave over the\""
            }
            object {
                id = 49
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"study of rhetoric, poetry, and the graces of language; and that I did\""
            }
            object {
                id = 50
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"not pace my house in my senatorial robes, or practise any similar\""
            }
            object {
                id = 51
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"affectation. I observed also the simplicity of style in his letters,\""
            }
            object {
                id = 52
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"particularly in that which he wrote to my mother from Sinuessa. I\""
            }
            object {
                id = 53
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"learned from him to be easily appeased, and to be readily reconciled\""
            }
            object {
                id = 54
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"with those who had displeased me or given cause of offence, so soon as\""
            }
            object {
                id = 55
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"they inclined to make their peace; to read with care; not to rest\""
            }
            object {
                id = 56
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"satisfied with a slight and superficial knowledge; nor quickly to\""
            }
            object {
                id = 57
                kind = "literal"
                scope = 0
                symbol = "\"assent to great talkers. I have him to thank that I met with the\""
            }
